{"availability":"available","full":"LEARNERS-PAL/Everythinmail-DEMO","name":"Everythinmail-DEMO","description":"This project aims to address this gap by developing an open-source API that can be used by developers to integrate email functionality into their applications quickly.","category":"Developer tools","language":"JavaScript","stars":3,"forks":0,"created":"2023-04-23T13:57:53Z","updated":"2024-02-29T13:17:36Z","branch":"master","homepage":"https://everything-mail.vercel.app/","topics":["api","email","open-source","react","reactjs"],"demo":"https://everything-mail.vercel.app/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T20:54:38.478Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T20:54:38.478Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T20:54:38.478Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T20:54:38.478Z","stars":3,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Email communication is an essential feature of many web and mobile applications, and developers often face challenges integrating email functionality into their applications. Currently, there are limited open-source options available for developers to use, which creates a need for an open-source API for sending and receiving emails that is easy to use and flexible. This project aims to address this gap by developing an open-source API that can be used by developers to integrate email functionality into their applications quickly.","Consider a case where a web developer is building an e-commerce platform that requires email notifications for order confirmation, order updates, and other customer-related communication. The developer can either develop a custom email sending solution or use an existing email service provider like Gmail, SendGrid, or MailChimp. However, custom solutions can be time-consuming to develop, while existing email service providers may have limitations in terms of customization, security, or cost.","By using our open-source email sending server API, the developer can easily integrate email functionality into their e-commerce platform with minimal effort. The API provides a simple and customizable solution that can be tailored to meet the specific needs of the project. Moreover, the use of TypeScript ensures that the code is robust and easy to maintain, while Nodemailer provides a reliable and secure email sending service."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/LEARNERS-PAL/Everythinmail-DEMO/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"4d1c0c34ba5676506b954b866d512cb02d66d84dbdf9928a9857eb795a4d43a2","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T20:54:38.614Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T20:54:38.614Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Email communication is an essential feature of many web and mobile applications, and developers often face challenges integrating email functionality into their applications. Currently, there are limited open-source options available for developers to use, which creates a need for an open-source API for sending and receiving emails that is easy to use and flexible. This project aims to address this gap by developing an open-source API that can be used by developers to integrate email functionality into their applications quickly.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/LEARNERS-PAL/Everythinmail-DEMO/blob/master/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"4d1c0c34ba5676506b954b866d512cb02d66d84dbdf9928a9857eb795a4d43a2","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/LEARNERS-PAL/Everythinmail-DEMO/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T20:54:38.614Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2024-02-29T13:17:36Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/LEARNERS-PAL/Everythinmail-DEMO/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T20:54:38.615Z","hash":"4d1c0c34ba5676506b954b866d512cb02d66d84dbdf9928a9857eb795a4d43a2","originalBytes":8508,"storedBytes":8508,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["email","api","data","xa0","developers","error","sending","project","should"